<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Relational" Version="10.0.12" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Agents.AI.OpenAI" Version="1.22.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Azure.AI.OpenAI" Version="2.9.0-beta.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="OpenAI" Version="2.13.0" />
    <!--
      These five move together. Microsoft.Agents.AI.* pulls Microsoft.Extensions.AI.Abstractions
      and OpenAI transitively, and the family is only safe at versions compiled against the SAME
      Abstractions — a mismatch is invisible to the compiler and throws TypeLoadException on the
      first agent run (see docs/anthropic-provider.md for the incident that established this).

      Verified compatible as a set, against assembly metadata rather than release notes:
        Microsoft.Agents.AI.* 1.22.0  -> Abstractions 10.10.0, OpenAI 2.13.0; 119 references into
                                         Microsoft.Extensions.AI, none dangling
        Azure.AI.OpenAI 2.9.0-beta.1  -> built against OpenAI 2.9.1 but unifies upward to 2.13.0:
                                         82 types and 145 member references, none missing
        Anthropic 12.49.0             -> Abstractions 10.5.1, unifies up to 10.10.0
        OpenAI 2.13.0                 -> exactly what Microsoft.Extensions.AI.OpenAI 10.10.0 wants,
                                         and still carries ChatCompletionOptions.ReasoningEffortLevel
                                         with its implicit conversion from string, which
                                         ReelForgeAgentBase.BuildChatOptions relies on

      Azure.AI.OpenAI is the laggard (2.9.0-beta.1 is the newest published) and is therefore the
      thing most likely to block the next bump of this set. Re-run the type/member reference scan
      against whatever OpenAI version the new Microsoft.Agents.AI wants before assuming it is fine.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Anthropic" Version="12.49.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.Abstractions" Version="10.0.12" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Binder" Version="10.0.12" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
